 experience flash flooding include...\nSan Isabel, Highway 165, Beulah, Highway 78, stream crossings, and\ncounty roads within and immediately downstream of the burn scar.\n\nThis includes the following high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.","ends":"2026-08-19T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89656b443b09a42855e7c4b3c2c85850f62c16a4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89656b443b09a42855e7c4b3c2c85850f62c16a4.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 19 at 6:42PM MDT until August 19 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Northern Aspen Acres Burn Scar in...\nEastern Custer County in southeastern Colorado...\nWest Central Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 945 PM MDT.\n\n* At 642 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Northern Aspen Acres Burn Scar. The expected\nrainfall rate is 0.5 to 0.75 inches in 1 hour. Flash flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly. Excessive rainfall over the\nburn scar will result in debris flow moving through the Red Creek,\nPeck Creek and Rock Creek Drainages. The debris flow can consist of\nrock, mud, vegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Northern Aspen Acres Burn\nScar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nNorthern Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nStream crossings and county roads within and immediately downstream\nof the burn scar.","ends":"2026-08-19T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dde0674d652d70203491013353b05ed28088a91c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dde0674d652d70203491013353b05ed28088a91c.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 19 at 6:02PM MDT until August 19 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 900 PM MDT.\n\n* At 602 PM MDT, trained weather spotters reported thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.5 and 1.5\ninches of rain have fallen. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Trained spotters reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPueblo, Pueblo Airport, Blende and Salt Creek.","ends":"2026-08-19T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4f9e010cd4e93fe36cb4ebed1e0021636ba8afb.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4f9e010cd4e93fe36cb4ebed1e0021636ba8afb.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 19 at 1:40PM MDT until August 19 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-19T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T23:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 192320 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 520 PM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Burn scar flash flooding and marginally severe storms possible this evening. - Daily afternoon showers and storms will continue into early next week, along with slowly warming temperatures. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH THURSDAY/... Issued at 1246 PM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T17:27:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 191727 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1127 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-201730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T18:47:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... No meteorological fire weather concerns across the district for t